  "solution": "The pattern followed in the given sets is:\n\n **(First term + Third term) ÷**** 2 + 2 = Second term**\n\nNow we apply the pattern on the given sets:\n\n(20, 16, 8)\n\n__**(20 + 8)**__ ÷ 2 + 2 = 16\n\n__**28 ÷ 2**__ + 2 = 16\n\n__**14 + 2**__ = 16 \n\n16 = 16\n\n(13, 20, 23)\n\n__(13 + 23)__ ÷ 2 + 2 = 20\n__36 ÷ 2__ + 2 = 20\n__18 + 2__ = 20 \n20 = 20\n\nNow we apply the pattern on the given options:\n\nOption 1) (19, 18, 21)\n\n__(19 + 21)__ ÷ 2 + 2 = 18\n__40 ÷ 2__ + 2 = 18\n__20 + 2__ = 18\n22 ≠ 18\n\nOption 2) (14, 18, 16)\n\n__(14 + 16)__ ÷ 2 + 2 = 18\n__30 ÷ 2__ + 2 = 18\n__15 + 2__ = 18\n17 ≠ 18\n\nOption 3) (32, 27, 18)\n\n__(32 + 18)__ ÷ 2 + 2 = 27\n__50 ÷ 2__ + 2 = 27\n__25 + 2__ = 27\n27 = 27\n\nOption 4) (13, 16, 13)\n\n__(13 + 13)__ ÷ 2 + 2 = 16\n__26 ÷ 2__ + 2 = 16\n__13 + 2__ = 16\n15 ≠ 16\n\nHence, the correct answer is “(32, 27, 18)”.",
